[results]
The available results headings report that the authors developed a potent clickable metformin surrogate, that metformin targets mitochondrial copper, and that copper is an essential component of epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition. The supplied excerpt does not provide numerical potency values, IC50/EC50 values, binding constants, fold changes, p values, or other quantitative outcomes, so specific quantitative results cannot be reported.
[context]
The experimental context is a cell-based and analytical-chemistry study using cell lines, chemical synthesis, fluorescence/cell imaging, western blotting, flow cytometry, copper/iron quantification, cyclic voltammetry, ROS and mitochondrial membrane potential assays, cell death assays, and ICP-MS. The supplied excerpt does not specify the exact cell lines, compound concentrations, instrument models, antibody targets, statistical tests, sample sizes, or whether KP-4 pancreatic cancer cells were used; therefore, those reproducibility details are not available from the provided text.
