- venue: Frontiers in Chemistry
- citation count: 24
[method]
The paper used an affinity-enrichment mass spectrometry workflow to identify HNE-modified mitochondrial proteins in rat liver mitochondria. Mitochondrial samples were exposed to HNE, and ARP-labeled HNE adducted proteins or peptides were enriched using streptavidin magnetic beads. Enriched samples were analyzed by SDS-PAGE and Western blotting, and by LC-MS label-free quantification against a reference mitochondrial proteome. A peptide-level enrichment step was also used to obtain site-specific ARP-HNE adduct information, and the enriched proteins/peptides were analyzed by Gene Ontology, KEGG pathway analysis, and hierarchical clustering. This is related to the proposed method because both approaches use a chemical affinity tag and streptavidin bead capture to enrich mitochondrial proteins for mass spectrometry, but the paper enriches HNE-ARP adducted proteins rather than biguanide-bound proteins and does not use metformin competition or a biguanide-pharmacophore control.
[results]
The workflow detected HNE-exposed mitochondrial proteome changes by SDS-PAGE and Western blotting and identified enriched ARP-HNE protein adducts by LC-MS label-free quantification. Peptide-level enrichment yielded site-specific ARP-HNE adduct sites, which were sorted by total occurrence of ARP-HNE sites. Linear regression and correlation were applied to evaluate the concentration-dependency of adduct accumulation on HNE concentration, with the regression coefficient representing the slope and the correlation coefficient representing linearity. The provided excerpt does not include specific protein names, fold changes, p-values, correlation coefficients, or statistical significance values.
[context]
Key experimental conditions included rat liver mitochondrial samples, HNE exposure, ARP labeling, streptavidin magnetic bead enrichment, SDS-PAGE/Western blotting, LC-MS label-free quantification, a reference mitochondrial proteome, and a concentration series used for regression and correlation analysis. The excerpt does not specify HNE concentrations, incubation times, bead amounts, MS instrument details, software, or statistical thresholds. The method relates to the research plan by demonstrating a streptavidin-based enrichment strategy for identifying chemically modified or probe-associated mitochondrial proteins, analogous to the planned BFB-streptavidin pull-down and metformin competition elution for identifying biguanide-binding mitochondrial targets such as ATP5I.
[end related work 1]






